The `cleanUp()` method periodically removes unused SMCs from the list based on whether they have any associated PDUs or not. This helps balance resource consumption and garbage collection.

This solution uses a lock-based approach for thread safety, which is simpler in terms of implementation but may impact performance in high concurrency scenarios due to contention over locks. To address this, consider using a lock-free algorithm such as linked lists with compare-and-swap (CAS) operations or other concurrent data structures when dealing with high concurrency levels in the 5G network environment.

For efficient memory utilization and latency minimization during high-load periods, consider optimizing the fetching of network status and UE mobility information from the external data source and adopting a suitable dynamic resizing strategy for the list of PDUs within each SMC. Lastly, this solution can scale horizontally by creating multiple instances of `SessionManagementContext` objects to distribute work across multiple threads or processes.']

