- The function uses a separate variable to store the length of the input string excluding the null terminator to avoid unnecessary overhead when calculating the index for appending padding or truncation.
- Memory is allocated dynamically using malloc, and any allocation failures are handled gracefully by returning NULL.
- To minimize memory usage, the function allocates only the required amount of memory for the output string.
- The function optimizes performance by iterating through the input string only once, regardless of whether padding or truncation is necessary.
