The function `reset_nfaapi_crc_pdu_array()` allows for resetting the array back to its initial state without leaks, though this comes at the overhead of freeing the entire array each time. The custom slab allocator minimizes fragmentation and improves memory usage, but may not be optimal in all cases due to the specific block sizes used for small and large blocks.

The code also uses a critical section (`pthread_mutex_lock()` and `pthread_mutex_unlock()`) to ensure thread safety when resizing or resetting the array, though this comes at the cost of slightly reduced performance due to lock contention.']

