The `traffic_list_push()` function adds an event to the list, ensuring that timestamps are generated in sequential order starting from the provided start time. The `traffic_list_filter()` and `traffic_list_compare()` functions allow filtering based on source IP, destination IP, or event type, as well as sorting by timestamp, packet size, or event type.

The code handles memory allocation failures gracefully and supports concurrent access by multiple threads using a mutex lock. It also includes a logging function to integrate with an external service for auditing purposes. Finally, the function is designed to be extensible, allowing for easy addition of new event types or data fields in the future.

Optimizations have been made to minimize memory usage when filtering large datasets and to ensure performance when handling large volumes of data without sacrificing readability and maintainability.']

